{"metadata":{"title":"Traffluent","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"symbolKind":"module","externalID":"Traffluent","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An event is a value conforming to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a value: tracking an event records it as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with its timestamp, the caller’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"SourceLocation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as one of the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"records","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Delivering is a chain of operators over that sequence: Afluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the default) gathers the records into batches, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"deliver(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hands each batch to every destination, as a lazy unit of work. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a plain sink, narrowed or transformed by its modifiers: ","type":"text"},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the consent categories it serves, ","type":"text"},{"code":"redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"droppingCallSite()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Consent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" delivers an event only once the user grants its ","type":"text"},{"code":"ConsentCategory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", holding it while undecided and dropping it when denied. ","type":"text"},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only queues an event, from any thread; a worker the tracker owns, never on the main actor, does the rest. A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes each record to disk as its worker reaches it and delivers what an earlier run left first. A property whose valid values are narrower than its type is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value, which satisfies its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Constraint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s from the moment it is made, or carries constraints declared with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the tracker’s worker rejects an event that breaks one before anything else, reporting each as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"RejectionReport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"rejectionReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On Apple platforms, SwiftUI views read the tracker from the environment and track what they do with view modifiers, and a screen’s events carry its ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","isActive":true},{"text":"). UIKit views and view controllers inherit it as a trait, the same value as SwiftUI’s, set on a window scene (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","isActive":true},{"text":"), and AppKit views find it up their responder chain (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","isActive":true},{"text":"); a control’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks an event through the tracker found when its action fires, so each scene or window can have its own. Screen views can track themselves once a window scene or window turns it on with ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreensAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which tracks ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as each screen’s view controller appears, without swizzling (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","isActive":true},{"text":"), and UIKit controls once a window scene turns it on with ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackControlsAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which tracks ","type":"text"},{"code":"ControlActivated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as a touch activates each control named by its accessibility identifier (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","isActive":true},{"text":"). On every platform, ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackLifecycle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and makes the tracker’s records durable as it leaves the foreground (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","isActive":true},{"text":"). A tracker given the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enricher stamps every event with its session’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a random identifier held in memory only, and starts a new session after a timeout of inactivity, tracking ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionEnded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionStarted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","isActive":true},{"text":"). A tracker given ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sampler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s keeps a seeded fraction of the events they apply to, event by event, or whole sessions with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", dropping the rest on its worker before they are held, written or delivered, reporting each drop as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SamplingDropReport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and stamping each kept record with its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SampleRateKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The standard enrichers, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.application()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"operatingSystem()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"locale()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"network()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"vendorIdentifier()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale, network connection and the platform’s identifier for vendor, each under a typed key, the static ones read once (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module but "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":", a product of its own for apps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that already use GRDB; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" macro derives an event’s conformances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and schema from its declaration and which alone builds swift-syntax; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exports those schemas as a JSON Schema tracking plan and checks the events against a committed one;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting"},{"type":"text","text":", which runs that check from an app’s tests; and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a test’s body a fresh tracker and returns what it tracked. Each module also has its own documentation and can be imported on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Traffluent","","struct SignedUp: Event {","    var plan: String","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"anchor":"Essentials"},{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/doc